# fields that lie in the Extension are read, asked for and stored outside loops and in one, in objects of five kinds:
# `bare` has no Extension . `low` and `high` have one that lacks the granules of the other . `full` holds them all . `one` holds a granule of bytes and one of narrow words with one slot filled in each
# m00 .. m09 are stored most often and take the room in the cell. m10 .. m23 hold numbers: eight bytes each. b0 .. b7 hold booleans: a byte each. r0 .. r3 hold objects: four bytes each
# `w` is listed by every maker and gets a value late: where it lies out of line its bytes do not say whether the object lists it
# again() reads a field, stores it through another name for what may be the same object, and reads it once more
# -- source: main.js
